1. [THEOREM] Denominator of $\frac{m}{n}$ is 1 iff $n \mid m$ for natural numbers
Module: Mathlib.Data.Rat.Lemmas
Name: Rat.den_div_natCast_eq_one_iff
Description: For any natural numbers $m$ and $n$ with $n \neq 0$, the denominator of the rational number $\frac{m}{n}$ is equal to $1$ if and only if $n$ divides $m$.
Signature:  (m n : ℕ) (hn : n ≠ 0) : ((m : ℚ) / n).den = 1 ↔ n ∣ m

2. [THEOREM] Denominator of Sum Divides LCM of Denominators
Module: Mathlib.Data.Rat.Lemmas
Name: Rat.add_den_dvd_lcm
Description: For any two rational numbers $q_1$ and $q_2$, the denominator of their sum $q_1 + q_2$ divides the least common multiple of the denominators of $q_1$ and $q_2$. In other words:
\[ \text{den}(q_1 + q_2) \mid \text{lcm}(\text{den}(q_1), \text{den}(q_2)) \]
Signature:  (q₁ q₂ : ℚ) : (q₁ + q₂).den ∣ q₁.den.lcm q₂.den

3. [THEOREM] Denominator of Zero is One
Module: Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs
Name: Rat.den_zero
Description: The denominator of the rational number $0$ is equal to $1$, i.e., $\text{den}(0) = 1$.
Signature:  : Rat.den 0 = 1

4. [THEOREM] Addition Formula for Rational Numbers in Terms of Numerators and Denominators
Module: Mathlib.Data.Rat.Lemmas
Name: Rat.add_num_den
Description: For any two rational numbers $q$ and $r$, their sum $q + r$ equals the fraction $\frac{q_\text{num} \cdot r_\text{den} + q_\text{den} \cdot r_\text{num}}{q_\text{den} \cdot r_\text{den}}$, where $q_\text{num}, r_\text{num}$ are the numerators and $q_\text{den}, r_\text{den}$ are the denominators of $q$ and $r$ respectively.
Signature:  (q r : ℚ) : q + r = (q.num * r.den + q.den * r.num : ℤ) /. (↑q.den * ↑r.den : ℤ)

5. [THEOREM] Denominator of Sum Divides Product of Denominators
Module: Mathlib.Data.Rat.Lemmas
Name: Rat.add_den_dvd
Description: For any two rational numbers $q_1$ and $q_2$, the denominator of their sum divides the product of their denominators, i.e., $(q_1 + q_2)_{\text{den}} \mid q_{1,\text{den}} \cdot q_{2,\text{den}}$.
Signature:  (q₁ q₂ : ℚ) : (q₁ + q₂).den ∣ q₁.den * q₂.den
