1. [THEOREM] Phragmen-Lindelöf Identity Principle in the Second Quadrant
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.PhragmenLindelof
Name: PhragmenLindelof.eqOn_quadrant_II
Description: Let $f, g : \mathbb{C} \to E$ be functions such that:

1. Both $f$ and $g$ are differentiable on the open second quadrant $\{z \in \mathbb{C} \mid \text{Re}(z) < 0 \text{ and } \text{Im}(z) > 0\}$ and continuous on its closure;
2. There exist constants $c_f < 2$, $B_f$ such that $\|f(z)\| = O(\exp(B_f |z|^{c_f}))$ as $|z| \to \infty$ in the second quadrant;
3. There exist constants $c_g < 2$, $B_g$ such that $\|g(z)\| = O(\exp(B_g |z|^{c_g}))$ as $|z| \to \infty$ in the second quadrant;
4. $f(x) = g(x)$ for all real $x \leq 0$;
5. $f(iy) = g(iy)$ for all real $y \geq 0$.

Then $f(z) = g(z)$ for all $z$ in the closed second quadrant $\{z \in \mathbb{C} \mid \text{Re}(z) \leq 0 \text{ and } \text{Im}(z) \geq 0\}$.
Signature:  (hdf : DiffContOnCl ℂ f (Iio 0 ×ℂ Ioi 0))
