Module: Mathlib.Data.DFinsupp.Defs
Name: DFinsupp.piecewise_single_erase
Description: For any dependently-typed function with finite support $x \in \Pi₀ i, \beta i$ and any index $i$, the piecewise combination of the single-element function (mapping $i$ to $x(i)$) and the erased function $x.\text{erase}\,i$ over the singleton set $\{i\}$ equals $x$. That is,
\[
(\text{single}\,i\,(x\,i)).\text{piecewise}\,(x.\text{erase}\,i)\,\{i\} = x
\]
