3. [DEFINITION] Piecewise finitely supported function
Module: Mathlib.Data.Finsupp.Basic
Name: Finsupp.piecewise
Description: Given a predicate $P$ on a type $\alpha$, and finitely supported functions $f \colon \{a // P a\} \to_0 M$ and $g \colon \{a // \neg P a\} \to_0 M$, the function $\text{piecewise}\ f\ g \colon \alpha \to_0 M$ is defined by case-splitting on $P a$:
\[
(\text{piecewise}\ f\ g)(a) = 
\begin{cases} 
f(\langle a, h \rangle) & \text{if } h : P a \\
g(\langle a, h \rangle) & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
\]
The support of $\text{piecewise}\ f\ g$ is the disjoint union of the supports of $f$ and $g$ mapped back to $\alpha$.
Signature:  (f : Subtype P →₀ M) (g : { a // ¬P a } →₀ M) : α →₀ M

4. [THEOREM] Pointwise Evaluation of Piecewise Defined Dependently-Typed Function
Module: Mathlib.Data.DFinsupp.Defs
Name: DFinsupp.piecewise_apply
Description: For any index $i \in \iota$, the value of the piecewise function $x.\mathrm{piecewise}\,y\,s$ at $i$ is equal to $x(i)$ if $i \in s$ and $y(i)$ otherwise. That is,
\[
(x.\mathrm{piecewise}\,y\,s)(i) = \begin{cases}
x(i) & \text{if } i \in s \\
y(i) & \text{otherwise.}
\end{cases}
\]
Signature:  (i : ι) : x.piecewise y s i = if i ∈ s then x i else y i

5. [DEFINITION] Case distinction for empty type vectors
Module: Mathlib.Data.TypeVec
Name: TypeVec.casesNil
Description: The function provides a case distinction for the empty type vector (0-length tuple of types). Given a function `f` defined on the empty type vector `Fin2.elim0`, it extends this function to any empty type vector `v` by casting (since all empty type vectors are propositionally equal).
Signature:  {β : TypeVec 0 → Sort*} (f : β Fin2.elim0) : ∀ v, β v

