2. [DEFINITION] Function extension along a map
Module: Mathlib.Logic.Function.Basic
Name: Function.extend
Description: Given functions $f : \alpha \to \beta$, $g : \alpha \to \gamma$, and $j : \beta \to \gamma$, the function $\text{extend}\,f\,g\,j : \beta \to \gamma$ is defined such that for any $b \in \beta$, if there exists $a \in \alpha$ with $f(a) = b$, then it returns $g(a)$ (where $a$ is chosen arbitrarily if there are multiple such $a$), and otherwise returns $j(b)$. 

This construction is mathematically meaningful when $g$ factors through $f$, meaning $f(a_1) = f(a_2)$ implies $g(a_1) = g(a_2)$. In particular, this holds automatically when $f$ is injective.

A typical use case is extending a function defined on a subtype to the entire type by specifying how to handle elements outside the subtype.
