Module: Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.AffineSpace.AffineMap
Name: AffineMap.homothetyAffine
Description: The function `homothetyAffine` maps a point $c$ in an affine space $P_1$ over a ring $k$ to an affine map from $k$ to the space of affine maps $P_1 \to_{k} P_1$. 

More precisely, for a fixed point $c \in P_1$, this function takes a scalar $r \in k$ and returns the homothety (scaling transformation) about $c$ with scale factor $r$, which is the affine map that sends any point $p \in P_1$ to $c + r \cdot (p - c)$.

The associated linear map of this affine map is the flipped version of the scalar multiplication bilinear map applied to the difference map $(id - \text{const}_c)$.
